<title>SPAIN: CNMV to remove suspension of BNP-Espana.</title>
<headline>CNMV to remove suspension of BNP-Espana.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's stock market watchdog CNMV said on Tuesday it was removing the suspension of BNP-Espana shares, effective Wednesday.</p>
<p>The unit is 97.4 percent owned by France's Banque National de Paris.</p>
<p>The shares were suspended in relation to a capital reduction that would reduce the share nominal to 73 from 75 pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
